<section class="panel form-panel"><div class="section-kicker">PAYMENT GATEWAY</div><h2>PayHub inline checkout & virtual accounts</h2><p class="muted">Accept card, transfer and dedicated virtual account payments directly inside the offering page. Pay with PayHub creates a pending payment notification automatically; treasury still performs final verification against the bank/gateway statement.</p><div class="payhub-status-row"><span class="badge <?= $payhubEnabled?'verified':($payhubReady?'pending':'rejected') ?>"><?= $payhubEnabled?'Connected':($payhubReady?'Keys saved · off':'Not configured') ?></span><small>Webhook URL · copy this into PayHub under API/Webhooks</small></div><div class="copy-field"><input id="payhub-webhook" value="<?= e($webhookUrl) ?>" readonly><button type="button" class="secondary copy-button" data-copy-target="payhub-webhook">Copy webhook</button></div><form method="post" class="form-grid"><?php hiddenAction('payhub_settings') ?><label>PayHub mode<select name="payhub_enabled"><option value="0" <?= !$payhubEnabled?'selected':'' ?>>Disabled — manual transfer only</option><option value="1" <?= $payhubEnabled?'selected':'' ?>>Enabled — inline checkout + virtual accounts</option></select></label><label>Public key<input name="payhub_public_key" maxlength="150" value="<?= e(setting($db,'payhub_public_key')) ?>" placeholder="pk_live_..." autocomplete="off"></label><label>Secret key<input type="password" name="payhub_secret_key" maxlength="200" value="<?= e(setting($db,'payhub_secret_key')) ?>" placeholder="sk_live_..." autocomplete="new-password"></label><label>Virtual account support<select name="payhub_virtual_accounts"><option value="1" <?= setting($db,'payhub_virtual_accounts')!=='0'?'selected':'' ?>>Request virtual accounts via PayHub inline</option><option value="0" <?= setting($db,'payhub_virtual_accounts')==='0'?'selected':'' ?>>Inline checkout only</option></select></label><label>Successful PayHub payments<select name="payhub_auto_approve"><option value="1" <?= setting($db,'payhub_auto_approve')!=='0'?'selected':'' ?>>Record and approve automatically after verified PayHub success</option><option value="0" <?= setting($db,'payhub_auto_approve')==='0'?'selected':'' ?>>Record only; require manual treasury approval</option></select></label><div class="notice small">Always verify the <code>X-Payhub-Signature</code> HMAC header before crediting payments. REMIT verifies webhook signatures automatically using your secret key.</div><button class="primary">Save PayHub settings</button></form><details class="sub-help"><summary>Setup checklist</summary><ul><li>Copy the webhook URL above into PayHub merchant dashboard.</li><li>Use live keys only after testing on PayHub sandbox if available.</li><li>Successful charges record gross credit and PayHub fees automatically when keys &amp; webhook signature verify.</li><li>Dedicated virtual account transfers settle at PayHub minus gateway fees; REMIT credits the church's full remittance toward its due balance while tracking PayHub fees and net settlement for treasury.</li></ul></details><?php $payhubLogs=PayHub::recentLogs(40); ?><details class="sub-help"><summary>Recent PayHub activity logs (latest <?= count($payhubLogs) ?> · secrets redacted)</summary><p class="muted small">Directory log file: <code>storage/logs/payhub.log</code></p><?php if(!$payhubLogs): ?><p class="muted small">No PayHub activity logged yet.</p><?php else: ?><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>TIME</th><th>EVENT</th><th>DETAILS</th></tr></thead><tbody><?php foreach($payhubLogs as $entry): ?><tr><td><small><?= e($entry['time']) ?></small></td><td><code><?= e($entry['event']) ?></code></td><td><small><code><?= e((string)json_encode($entry['payload'],JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES)) ?></code></small></td></tr><?php endforeach ?></tbody></table></div><?php endif ?></details></section>
<section class="panel form-panel"><h2>Email password reset</h2><p class="muted">Email code recovery is enabled by default on the login page. Use an authorized sender mailbox on your hosting domain. Your server’s PHP mail service must be configured; mail acceptance does not guarantee inbox delivery. Back up the database before first enabling this feature.</p><form method="post"><?php hiddenAction('password_reset_settings') ?><label>Password recovery<select name="password_reset_enabled"><option value="1">Enabled (default)</option><option value="0" <?= setting($db,'password_reset_enabled')==='0'?'selected':'' ?>>Disabled</option></select></label><label>Sender email address<input type="email" name="password_reset_sender" maxlength="150" value="<?= e(setting($db,'password_reset_sender')) ?>" placeholder="no-reply@your-domain.example"><small>Leave blank to use the installation notification email, or the first admin email.</small></label><button class="primary">Save password reset settings</button></form></section>
